# diff-workflows

> Pick the right diff view for the job.
> Full guide: ~/obsidian-vault/Agent/Diff Workflows.md

- Review the agent's proposed rewrite and merge hunks by hand:
`nvim -d {{original.md}} {{original.agent.md}}`

- Just read a proposed rewrite, no editing:
`diff -u {{original.md}} {{original.agent.md}} | delta`

- Semantic diff: ignores reformatting, shows only structural change:
`GIT_EXTERNAL_DIFF=difft git diff`

- Semantic diff of two specific files:
`difft {{old}} {{new}}`

- Everything uncommitted, side panel inside nvim:
`:DiffviewOpen`

- Only the last commit:
`:DiffviewOpen HEAD~1`

- History of the current file:
`:DiffviewFileHistory %`

- History of the whole repo:
`:DiffviewFileHistory`

- Stage hunks, browse log, resolve conflicts in a TUI:
`lazygit`

- Diff two arbitrary files (works untracked, goes through delta):
`git diff --no-index {{a}} {{b}}`

- Jump between changes inside a diff:
`]c` (next) / `[c` (previous)

- Pull a hunk across in vimdiff:
`:diffget` / `:diffput`
